  "about": "Plan questions and Needs you (docs/design/plan-asks.md, crates/proto/src/view/plan_asks.rs). Each case is one workspace snapshot: `now` (epoch ms), `online` (device ids whose host is reachable; any other device is offline), `chats` (registry chat rows, only the fields the rule reads: id, deviceId, archived, child.parentChatId), `sessions` (registry session rows exactly as the host writes them, times in epoch ms; `asking` = the open question, absent on old hosts) and `work` (one bot_work row of bot `b`, with `steered`). Expected: `needsYou` = BotRecords::needs_you(\"b\") with the plan-question rule, each item with the chat that asks (`askingChatId`: the plan chat itself or a child under it), that chat's `asking.requestId` (null on old rows) and `offline` (its host is not in `online`: shown as \"Waiting for its device\"); `steps` = BotWork::settled_steps on the same rule; `indicators` = effective_indicator per session row (an open question never ages out). The Rust runner is crates/proto/tests/plan_asks_vectors.rs; the iPhone twin and the Worker run these too.",
